Your response has a maximum of exactly 1 attained by exactly one observation, which is the signature of a response divided by its own observed maximum. Dividing by an extreme order statistic correlates every observation, discards the uncertainty in the divisor and biases ECx estimates upwards; it also forces one observation outside the open support of the Beta family. Prefer fitting the raw response and reading effective concentrations off the fitted curve with ecx(type = "absolute"), which is already the default. See Ritz et al. (2026) doi:10.1007/s10651-025-00698-y, and ?ecx for what to do instead.
